    "title": "Why Michiganders Should Be Rubbing Soap Around Their Doors This Summer - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Michigan\nWhy Michiganders Should Be Rubbing Soap Around Their Doors This Summer\nBy Laura Hardy,\n6 hours agoIf you’ve stepped outside lately and spotted dozens of tiny ant hills scattered across your yard, you’re not alone. It’s officially ant season here in Michigan, and if your house is like mine, you’re seeing their annual takeover begin. These little pests always seem to know just how to sneak inside my house, marching in through windowsills, under doors, and anywhere else they can find a crumb as soon as it gets above 60 degrees.",
